# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Bun auto-loads .env at daemon startup.
#
# AI Pass release configuration (maintainers / first-party builds only). The value is a PUBLIC
# OAuth client id, but it is supplied through protected build/runtime configuration and must never
# be committed, printed, or bundled into the PWA. It is used only in OAuth protocol requests.
# Source builds without it fail closed at login and keep every existing provider available.
# REPOYETI_AIPASS_CLIENT_ID=
#
# BYOK AI remains available: add a provider key in Settings → AI. There's no bundled key — Groq
# revokes any key committed to a public repo, so a shipped one is dead on arrival. Groq is the
# suggested provider (free + fast, ~30s):
#   https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# No environment variables are required to run RepoYeti.
